            <ArticleTitle>Retroperitoneal hemorrhage after cardiac catheterization causing a diagnostic dilemma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>461-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Emergency coronary angioplasty is being increasingly performed these days. This procedure may be associated with complications. We report a case of massive retroperitoneal hemorrhage after coronary angioplasty that posed a diagnostic dilemma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
